  "challenge": "This is decidable as REJECT without a human queue. Gadgets Co. is an active master vendor on contracted Net 30 since 2020-07-22 with an exact catalog price match on GadgetX, and get_prior_invoice shows INV-1002 is not a duplicate—but TM-003’s own policy rationale frames a due date on or before the invoice date as a coercion tactic, and here due_date equals invoice_date while TM-001 quantifies a full 30-day miss versus Net 30 (not a one- or two-day typo). get_vendor_invoice_history further shows zero prior invoices and $0 history for this payee in the audit store, so there is no successful payment track record to lean on, and IN-003 bills 20 units against standing stock of 5 with no note explaining backorder or incoming supply. PO-001 already blocks auto-approval by policy; stacking the coercion-flagged due date, the empty payee history, and the unexplained overstock makes rejection pending a corrected due date and a proper approval path the evidence-backed call, not an open-ended escalate.",
  "proposed_outcome": "REJECT",
  "cites_finding_codes": ["TM-003", "TM-001", "IN-003", "PO-001"]
}
